{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And I have given you one portion above your brothers.</b> After he blessed the sons of Joseph and made them two tribes, he turned back to Joseph and said to him: Behold, I am dying, and Elohim will be with you in the exile, to deliver you from every trouble, and you shall be fruitful and multiply greatly, and He will restore you to the land of your fathers to possess it. And I have already given you in that land the one portion that is in my hand to give, and it is the portion of the firstborn, for you to have in it more than your brothers, from the day I took it from the hand of the Amorite with my sword and with my bow. And all of this is conciliation toward Joseph and his love for him, for he informed him that he had given him the birthright, so that his sons from now on would be blessed to become two tribes both in the banners of the wilderness and in the dedication of the princes, and also the portion that belonged to him in the inheritance he gave him, that he would merit it when they conquer the land with sword and bow and in war. And behold, he said to him: I have done with you all the good that I was able to do for you at the time I was able to do it, for it is not within Jacob's authority in the land except for one portion (שכם), for it is not in his power to take away from any one of his sons his inheritance; only the birthright was his to give to whomever was good in his eyes, and behold, he gave it to him." "And the sense of <b>from the hand of the Amorite</b> is that Israel took the land initially from the hand of the Amorite, for Sihon and Og were the two kings of the Amorite, and the first and great war that they had in the conquest of the land was for the sons of Joseph against the Amorite — it is the war of Joshua with them, and through them the great miracle was performed, as it is written (Joshua 10:12): \"Then Joshua spoke to YHWH on the day YHWH delivered the Amorite before the children of Israel,\" etc. And from the hand of the Amorite was the portion and inheritance of the sons of Joseph, as it is written (Numbers 32:39): \"And the sons of Machir son of Manasseh went to Gilead and took it and dispossessed the Amorite who was in it,\" and the sons of Ephraim also inherited within the border of the Amorite, as it is written (Judges 1:35): \"And the Amorite refused to dwell in Mount Heres in Aijalon and in Shaalbim, and the hand of the house of Joseph prevailed, and they became tributary.\"" "And the sense of <b>with my sword and with my bow</b> is that the land would not be conquered for them except with sword and bow; he alludes to what Scripture says (Joshua 11:19–20): \"There was not a city that made peace with the children of Israel except the Hivite, inhabitants of Gibeon; all the rest they took in battle, for it was from YHWH to harden their hearts to meet Israel in battle in order to destroy them.\" And he attributes the sword and the bow to himself, for his merit is what makes war prevail for them, and it is he who fights for them, not they themselves, in the manner that Scripture says (Psalms 44:4): \"For not by their sword did they possess the land, and their arm did not save them, but Your right hand and Your arm and the light of Your countenance, for You favored them.\" And this is by the merit of the fathers, for by way of truth, \"Your right hand\" — for Abraham; \"and Your arm\" — for Isaac; \"and the light of Your countenance\" — for Jacob. And it seems likely to me further that Jacob did as the prophets would do: he stretched out his hand with the sword toward the land of the Amorite and shot arrows there so that it would be conquered for his sons, in the manner that Elisha did: \"And he placed his hands upon the hands of the king, and Elisha said: Shoot! And he shot\" (II Kings 13:16). And even though Scripture did not relate this, it alludes to it in this verse. And it is possible that this is the reason he said \"I took,\" for from that time the land was acquired for his sons."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:54.820288043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}